# Coded slab heap (0x64000000, 7MB) is shared with the DPU display framebuffers
# (1280x720x2 double-buffered ~3.6MB). The encoded-data manager allocates a
# 20-deep pool of this size; 256KB*20=5MB no longer fits beside the display
# buffers and the H264 manager malloc fails (-> bk_mem_slab_free assert).
# 960x540 H264 frames are <100KB, so 128KB*20=2.5MB fits with margin.
